{"id":"design-twitter","title":"Design Twitter","difficulty":"Medium","pattern":"Design","tags":["Hash Table","Linked List","Design","Heap / Priority Queue"],"companies":{"google":2,"apple":2,"meta":3,"amazon":4,"microsoft":2},"kind":"design","class_name":"Twitter","description":"Design a tiny social network with posts, follows and a news feed.\n\n- `Twitter()` creates the service.\n- `postTweet(userId, tweetId)` publishes a tweet. Each `tweetId` is unique.\n- `getNewsFeed(userId)` returns the ids of the **10 most recent** tweets written by the user or by anyone they follow, newest first. Fewer than 10 are returned if that is all there is.\n- `follow(followerId, followeeId)` makes the first user follow the second.\n- `unfollow(followerId, followeeId)` undoes a follow. Unfollowing someone you do not follow does nothing.\n\nUsers always see their own tweets in their feed, and user ids are created implicitly the first time they appear.","examples":[{"input":"[\"Twitter\",\"postTweet\",\"getNewsFeed\",\"follow\",\"postTweet\",\"getNewsFeed\",\"unfollow\",\"getNewsFeed\"]\n[[],[1,5],[1],[1,2],[2,6],[1],[1,2],[1]]","output":"[null,null,[5],null,null,[6,5],null,[5]]","explanation":"After following user 2, user 1 sees tweet 6 (newer) before their own tweet 5. After unfollowing, only tweet 5 remains."},{"input":"[\"Twitter\",\"getNewsFeed\",\"follow\",\"postTweet\",\"getNewsFeed\"]\n[[],[9],[9,9],[9,1],[9]]","output":"[null,[],null,null,[1]]","explanation":"A brand-new user has an empty feed. Following yourself must not duplicate your own tweets."}],"constraints":["1 <= userId, followerId, followeeId <= 500","0 <= tweetId <= 10^4","All tweet ids are distinct","At most 3 * 10^4 calls in total"],"hints":["Stamp every tweet with a global, increasing counter so recency can be compared across users.","Store each user's tweets in a list (newest at the end) and their followees in a set.","The feed is a k-way merge of the followees' tweet lists: push each followee's most recent twee